message: "If you cite this computational research thesis, please use the metadata below. No DOI is minted here; do not invent one."
type: thesis
title: "Hybrid occult mode switches versus chain-recurrent components on a joint hybrid–smooth field"
authors:
  - family-names: Ogbonna
    given-names: Kelechi Emeka
    email: kelechiogbonna300@gmail.com
    alias: cloudynirvana
abstract: >-
  On a joint hybrid–smooth toy, do hybrid occult mode-switch observables
  align with chain-recurrent components from a complete Lyapunov construction,
  or can switches fall inside a single recurrent region? A planar
  tumour–effector field has an unstable focus and a periodic orbit of period
  19.876. Immune and angiogenic guards meet that orbit at four points, each
  separated from the focus, and each of those points falls in the interior of
  one collocation-defect component on three grids. A cycling guard misses the
  orbit and is crossed in the transient complement. The rebuilt orbital
  derivative is positive on 47.6 percent of the orbit, so the defect is not a
  certified Conley set. Not a medical device. No cure.
keywords:
  - hybrid systems
  - occult residual disease
  - chain recurrence
  - complete Lyapunov function
  - collocation
  - Filippov
  - toy model
  - research-only
